From: aiden build <build@aiden.local>
Subject: [PATCH] adb_wifi: restore mDNS pairing (address-first)

Re-enable mdns-based pairing service lookup that nmeum's 0027 patch
removed (replaced the `if (true)` short-circuit). Add the missing
<android-base/stringprintf.h> include for the restored StringPrintf.

IMPORTANT divergence from upstream AOSP: parse the host as a literal
address FIRST, and only fall back to mdns_get_pairing_service_info()
when it is not a valid address:port. The pairing handler runs on its
own service thread (create_service_thread), while the mDNS service
registries are mutated by the discovery callbacks on the main fdevent
thread. Reading those registries from the pair thread for an explicit
IP (as upstream does unconditionally) races with a concurrent
push_back/erase during '_adb-tls-pairing' discovery and crashes the
adb server (client sees "protocol fault (couldn't read status
length)"). Address-first keeps explicit-IP pairing off the registries
entirely; mDNS-name pairing still works.

Auto-connect after pairing is intentionally NOT restored: it reads
sAdbSecureConnectServices from this same thread and would reintroduce
the identical race. Users can 'adb connect' explicitly.

Aiden-local patch (re-enables mDNS that nmeum disabled for the client).
---
--- a/vendor/core/adb/client/adb_wifi.cpp
+++ b/vendor/core/adb/client/adb_wifi.cpp
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <adb/crypto/x509_generator.h>
 #include <android-base/file.h>
 #include <android-base/parsenetaddress.h>
+#include <android-base/stringprintf.h>
 #include "client/pairing/pairing_client.h"
 
 #include "adb_auth.h"
@@ -179,16 +180,25 @@
 
 void adb_wifi_pair_device(const std::string& host, const std::string& password,
                           std::string& response) {
-    if (true) {
-        // Check the address for a valid address and port.
+    // If |host| is a literal "address:port", pair with it directly and do not
+    // consult mDNS. Only fall back to an mDNS service-name lookup when |host|
+    // is not a valid network address (e.g. an mDNS instance name). This keeps
+    // explicit-IP pairing off the mDNS service registries, which are mutated
+    // by the discovery thread on the main fdevent thread and are not safe to
+    // read concurrently from this pairing service thread.
+    std::optional<MdnsInfo> mdns_info;
+    {
         std::string parsed_host;
         std::string err;
         int port = -1;
         if (!android::base::ParseNetAddress(host, &parsed_host, &port, nullptr, &err)) {
-            response = "Failed to parse address for pairing: " + err;
-            return;
-        }
-        if (port <= 0 || port > 65535) {
+            // Not a literal address; try to resolve it as an mDNS pairing service name.
+            mdns_info = mdns_get_pairing_service_info(host);
+            if (!mdns_info.has_value()) {
+                response = "Failed to parse address for pairing: " + err;
+                return;
+            }
+        } else if (port <= 0 || port > 65535) {
             response = "Invalid port while parsing address [" + host + "]";
             return;
         }
@@ -222,7 +232,10 @@
 
     PairingResultWaiter waiter;
     std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lock(waiter.mutex_);
-    if (!client->Start(host,
+    if (!client->Start(mdns_info.has_value()
+                               ? android::base::StringPrintf("%s:%d", mdns_info->addr.c_str(),
+                                                             mdns_info->port)
+                               : host,
                        waiter.OnResult, &waiter)) {
         response = "Failed: Unable to start pairing client.";
         return;
